  "description": "# LSC-01 | Fun 001 | Queue Luma Guest for SF Campaign Sync\n\n**📋 Ticket:** [Luma guests → Salesforce campaign members](https://brightdata-group.monday.com/boards/8667788707/pulses/13343839880)\n\n---\n\n**TRIGGER:** Called async by `Webhook: Luma-to-HubSpot Guest Sync` (end of the not-ignored path)\n\n**PURPOSE:** Queue every Luma guest registration for the hourly Salesforce campaign sync.\n\n**FLOW:**\n1. Look up the row by `luma_guest_id` + `luma_url_slug` → PostgreSQL\n2. Exists → re-queue (Pending, attempts 0, `next_attempt_at` = now + 1h); else insert\n\n**DB / TABLES:** `marketing.luma_sf_campaign_queue` (read/write)\n**UPSTREAM:** Webhook: Luma-to-HubSpot Guest Sync  \n**DOWNSTREAM:** none\n\n## Important logic\n- One row per guest + event (unique key). A webhook retry or status change re-queues the same row.\n- First sync attempt 1h after the last webhook, so HubSpot → SF can create the Lead.\n- Fire-and-forget: calls System Error Handling itself on failure.\n",
  "name": "LSC-01 | Fun 001 | Queue Luma Guest for SF Campaign Sync",
  "private": false,
  "version": 2
